# function P() { this.x = 1; }  Object.defineProperty(P.prototype, name, { set(v) { } });  const kMark = Symbol("mark");  const p = new P();  p[kMark] = 1;  p.f = 1;
# Nobody knows `name`, so `f` may be the name of that setter: with a slot each `p.f = 1` would find it empty and go upward, and no table would remember the answer. So `f` gets none.
# Whoever lays names that nobody knows goes through the names of another object, and a symbol that the program makes is hardly among them: `socket[kRequest] = request` below Readable.prototype, six stores a request of node:http.
# RUN: link fields mechanisms=all
# CHECK: field L0.0 "x"
# CHECK: field L0.1 symbol("mark")@m0:0 appended
# CHECK-NOT: field L0.2

